Subject: [PATCH] Floating square debug: frame-diff metric + per-method error-history sparkline

Implements the approved Stage-2 plan from
docs/checkpoints/floating-square-motion-smoothness-metric.md (Stage 1
architecture + the user's four resolved decisions: center metric
scalarizes as |centroid − pos|, area as |signed error|, history
samples only when the square actually moved — manual mouse movement
counts — and all four method slots keep history across candidate
switches so the display just switches).

- coverage.rs: `frame_diff_xor` / `frame_diff_pane` (`#[doc(hidden)]`
  debug surface) — rendered change per frame on the same lattice and
  SX*SY denominator as `coverage_error`, so the value is directly
  comparable to the ideal-square xor; the pane lights differing
  samples over the same 2x2 window crop as the other metric panes.
  Two pane_tests added (identical → 0/empty; pane ≡ number over the
  crop; change grows with displacement), plus the grid-size guard.
- floating_square_debug.rs: METRICS 6 → 7 (+ `frame`). The metric
  computation moved out of method_section's inline match into
  `metric_report` (single source of truth) returning pane + value +
  the history scalar; render_animation_frame now computes all four
  method slots every frame (displayed rows reuse pane/value, all four
  numbers feed the sparklines), so a candidate switch only changes
  which slots are displayed and the shared y-axis (max over all live
  slots, floor 1e-6) stays stable across switches. `record_history`
  appends only when pos changed since the last sample (parked redraws
  and metric/candidate switches append nothing); prev_renders updates
  on every rendered frame so frame-diff always compares against the
  immediately previous render (n/a only before the first frame).
  New 4th method-row column: SPARKLINE_LEN=32 blocks (▁▂▃▄▅▆▇█,
  EIGHTH_BLOCKS_FROM_BOTTOM) right-aligned with a scale legend.
  Three bin tests: sparkline level mapping/alignment, history
  semantics (motion-only appends, caps, metric-change resets,
  candidate-switch preserves), and metric_report scalars.

Verification: terminal_rendering 154 passed / 0 failed (lib 141, bin
4, integration 9); workspace 489 / 0. Method rows measure 132 visible
columns; piped frames show the sparkline growing one block per frame
with the shared max tracking. A fresh recompile also surfaced a
